EXT. LIFE RAFT - OPEN OCEAN - DAY

A yellow inflatable raft rides a long gray swell. The horizon is a razor line. Sun beats down on a torn canopy. A water jug, a flare tin, a coil of rope.

ANSELMO TRUJILLO-REYES, forties, a cargo ship engineer, lies on his back on the floor of the raft, cracked lips, shirt over his head. Across from him sits ODALIE BRANDVOLD, thirties, a deckhand, her hair salted into rope, clutching the water jug to her chest.

ODALIE
(to herself)
Don't look. Don't look at the horizon. Don't count the days.

ANSELMO
You're talking.

ODALIE
I'm not talking.

ANSELMO
You're muttering.

ODALIE
Then I'm muttering.

She tilts the jug. Anselmo's eyes follow it. She lowers it without drinking.

ANSELMO
How much left?

ODALIE
Two inches.

ANSELMO
Two inches of what? Two inches in the jug or two inches in the bottle?

ODALIE
Two inches in the jug. The bottle's empty.

ANSELMO
When did that happen?

ODALIE
Yesterday. While you were asleep.

ANSELMO
You drank it?

ODALIE
I split it. Four sips each.

ANSELMO
I don't remember mine.

ODALIE
You were out.

Anselmo pulls the shirt off his face and stares at the sky. Gulls wheel above.

ANSELMO
Birds.

ODALIE
Yes.

ANSELMO
Birds mean land.

ODALIE
Birds mean fish.

ANSELMO
Land's close.

ODALIE
Don't.

She stands, rocking the raft, and shades her eyes. She cups her hands around her mouth and shouts at the empty sea.

ODALIE (CONT'D)
(to the horizon)
HEY! HEY! OVER HERE!

Nothing. Waves slap the rubber. She sits. Anselmo closes his eyes.

ANSELMO
Who are you calling?

ODALIE
Whoever's listening.

ANSELMO
Nobody's listening.

ODALIE
Somebody's always listening.

ANSELMO
That's God.

ODALIE
That's a plane.

Anselmo opens his eyes. Far above, a tiny silver glint crosses the blue. Odalie lunges for the flare tin, tears it open, and fires. A red streak shoots up, trailing smoke. They both stare after it.

ANSELMO
(whispering)
Did they see?

ODALIE
(whispering)
I don't know.

The plane glints, banks, and begins a slow, wide circle. Odalie drops the flare gun. Anselmo, laughing and sobbing, props himself on one elbow and raises his hand. She grips the jug, takes one long drink, then passes it to him.

ODALIE (CONT'D)
Finish it.
